  "notes": "Sony BRAVIA 4K UR2 (device BRAVIA_UR2_4K, MediaTek)\nAndroid 10 (Android TV, API 29), build QTG3.200305.006.S97 662301 (US UC firmware and EU retail KD-55XG9505)\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/sony-bravia-4k-ur2/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/sony-bravia-4k-ur2/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nStock launcher: com.google.android.tvlauncher (the restore.sh default is correct).\nLive TV / tuner app: com.sony.dtv.tvx (set it as live_tv_package in the launcher's config.xml).\nKeep the com.sony.dtv.tvinput.* services, com.sony.dtv.braviasync*, com.sony.dtv.tvapi,\ncom.sony.dtv.sonysystemservice and the Sony settings apps: they drive HDMI, the tuner, Bravia Sync\nand the remote.\nAlready disabled at the factory: com.sony.dtv.b2b.vendorprotocol, com.sony.dtv.b2b.softap,\nscrenmirroring.com.\n\nApplied on US firmware (dock: Netflix, YouTube, Disney+, ZEE5) and re-confirmed on an EU retail\nKD-55XG9505 (BRAVIA_UR2_4K_EU) with the Apple TV style launcher (dock: Netflix, Prime Video,\nYouTube, Spotify). HDMI 1-4/eARC, TVX tuner, Bravia Sync, and remote control verified across reboots.\ntracking / ads / recommendations",
